GTERM(1)

NAME
    gterm - graphical PTY terminal

SYNOPSIS
    gterm [COMMAND [ARG...]]

DESCRIPTION
    Open an 80 by 30 terminal in a 640 by 480 RGB565 window. With no
    command, run sh. Requires the RVM MMU profile and launcher --visual.
    One graphics window is available in this milestone.

    The terminal supports ANSI cursor movement, colours, scrolling,
    editing and alternate screen. Ctrl-C and Ctrl-Z go to the foreground
    PTY job. Use jobs, bg and fg in sh. Exit the shell to close its terminal.

    Closing the host window hangs up the child session; Riplix keeps
    running. Start gterm again from the original console. Use shutdown
    to save the disk and stop the operating system.

LIMITS
    Fixed size, bitmap font, basic US keyboard. No Unicode, clipboard,
    scrollback, mouse reporting or dynamic resize yet.
